# Application Environment Configuration

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Salon360 Online Booking API — Integration Credentials
# Store: storeId 868 / orgId 555
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️  SECURITY: These credentials grant FULL access to the store's
#     booking API.  NEVER expose them in client-side / browser code.
#
#     For local development the Vite dev-server proxy forwards
#     /salon360-api/* to the real API base URL and injects the
#     x-api-key header on the server side so the secret never
#     reaches the browser.
#
#     For production: deploy a backend proxy (Cloudflare Worker,
#     Next.js API route, Express server, etc.) that reads these
#     variables and forwards requests.  Then set
#     VITE_SALON360_PROXY_URL to your proxy's URL.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

SALON360_CLIENT_KEY=64afb73f-ec89-4d1f-b639-914960f34f47
SALON360_CLIENT_SECRET=b3c52a47-845c-40af-bb43-37e52df12ce7

# Combined header value: <CLIENT_KEY>:<CLIENT_SECRET>
SALON360_API_KEY=64afb73f-ec89-4d1f-b639-914960f34f47:b3c52a47-845c-40af-bb43-37e52df12ce7

# Real Salon360 API base URL
SALON360_API_BASE=https://api.salon360app.com/api/online-booking/v1/external/booking

# (Optional) Override the proxy URL the browser-side code calls.
# Defaults to /salon360-api (handled by Vite proxy in dev).
# In production set this to your backend proxy URL.
# VITE_SALON360_PROXY_URL=https://your-backend.example.com/salon360-proxy
